hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1584","Narrated by Muhammad bin Bashar, narrated by Yahya bin Saeed, narrated by Hisham bin Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Qatada. H. Bundar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Arouba. H, Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi said: Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari led us in prayer, and when he turned, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us, and explained to us Our Sunnah, and he taught us our prayer, and he said: “So when the imam says “Allahu Akbar,” say “Allahu Akbar,” and when he says: “Not those with anger upon them, nor those who have gone astray,” then say: “Ameen.” He loves you. \God.\"" Abu Bakr said: This news is based on ensuring that the follower is secured when the imam finishes reciting the Fatihah of the Book"","" even if his imam does not secure it out of ignorance. Or forgetfulness"""""
